<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Waldburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1429 CE – 1806 CE (approx.) · capital Wolfegg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The upper Swabian territory of the Truchsesses of Waldburg, whose Georg, the 'Bauernjörg', crushed the Peasants' War of 1525.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The lords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-waldburg">Waldburg</a> near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-ravensburg">Ravensburg</a> served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> as imperial stewards (Truchsess). In the 14th and 15th centuries they acquired lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfegg">Wolfegg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeil-castle">Zeil</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-waldsee">Waldsee</a>, and after a division in 1429 the branches of the family built up a cluster of lordships and counties in upper Swabia.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georg-truchsess-von-waldburg">Georg III, Truchsess of Waldburg</a>, commanded the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-league">Swabian League</a> that crushed the peasant revolt in 1525, earning the nickname 'Bauernjörg'. The family remained Catholic and supplied churchmen such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-truchsess-von-waldburg">Otto Truchsess von Waldburg</a>, cardinal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-augsburg">Augsburg</a>. Repeated partitions created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-waldburg">Waldburg</a>-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfegg">Wolfegg</a>, Waldburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeil-castle">Zeil</a> and other lines, which ranked as imperial counts from the 17th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Mediatised in 1806, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-waldburg">Waldburg</a> lands passed mainly to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-wurttemberg">Kingdom of Württemberg</a>, with some under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. The princely families of Waldburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeil-castle">Zeil</a> and Waldburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfegg">Wolfegg</a> still own their castles and estates.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-waldburg.jpg" alt="County of Waldburg" width="320" height="343"><figcaption>Image: Unbekannt / Vektorisiert von User:Flow2 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wappen_Waldburg.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1429 CE – 1806 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Wolfegg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Georg III Truchsess von Waldburg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swabian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Truchsess von Waldburg, Waldburg-Zeil, Waldburg-Wolfegg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1618&amp;focus=county-of-waldburg" aria-label="County of Waldburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4908 503 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Waldburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5228 759L5229 694M5228 759L5212 730"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5212 730h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5228 759h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5228 759h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Wolfegg. <a href="/atlas?year=1618&amp;focus=county-of-waldburg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
